For the stage-level scale, the thresholds are computed from all non-idle stage-level displacement values: γ 1 stage = 0.01998 , γ 2 stage = 0.04693 . \gamma^{\mathrm{stage}}_{1}=0.01998,\qquad\gamma^{\mathrm{stage}}_{2}=0.04693. The scale label of a non-idle stage s s is defined as c stage ​ ( s ) = { Low , D stage ​ ( s ) < γ 1 stage , Medium , γ 1 stage ≤ D stage ​ ( s ) < γ 2 stage , High , D stage ​ ( s ) ≥ γ 2 stage . c_{\mathrm{stage}}(s)=\begin{cases}\text{Low},&D_{\mathrm{stage}}(s)<\gamma^{\mathrm{stage}}_{1},\\
\text{Medium},&\gamma^{\mathrm{stage}}_{1}\leq D_{\mathrm{stage}}(s)<\gamma^{\mathrm{stage}}_{2},\\
\text{High},&D_{\mathrm{stage}}(s)\geq\gamma^{\mathrm{stage}}_{2}.\end{cases}
